# M7 (TODO-0231): the todos counter used to match every right-lined "TODO",
# including TODO-NNNN unit ids and test fixture ids — so each test-heavy unit
# raised the baseline by hand. It now counts ONLY real debt markers: TODO:,
# FIXME and XXX introduced by a comment prefix (#, //, /*, *, --), or a bare
# marker at the start of a line. Unit ids in code, strings and docs are not
# debt. Documented recalculation: 6633 -> 0 (the repo carries no real debt
# marker; every counted line was an identifier).
# Z2 (REVIEW виток 6): `TODO(owner):` is debt too — the parenthesised scope
# between the marker and the colon does not change the meaning, so the
# counter reads an optional `(…)` group there (same for FIXME/XXX).
# ARCH (TODO-0231): the marker alternation lives ONCE (`DEBT=` in the
# command); the three prefix branches only decide WHERE a marker may start
# (line-start comment, inline comment, bare line start). Z2 had to edit three
# copies — that is the drift this collapse removes.
# Line-count numbers in the comments below are refreshed by
# `sh scripts/ratchet.sh --update` from `@lines <path> (<count> lines)`
# annotations — no manual doc drift.
todos	DEBT='TODO[[:space:]]*(\([^)]*\))?[[:space:]]*:|FIXME[[:space:]]*(\([^)]*\))?[[:space:]]*([^A-Za-z0-9_]|$)|XXX[[:space:]]*(\([^)]*\))?[[:space:]]*([^A-Za-z0-9_]|$)'; git ls-files --cached --others --exclude-standard | grep -v '^\.ratchet' | grep -v '^BACKLOG\.md$' | grep -v '^BACKLOG-archive\.md$' | grep -v '^docs/audit-' | xargs grep -cIE "(^[[:space:]]*(#|//|/\*|\*|--)[[:space:]]*|[[:space:]](#|//)[[:space:]]*|^[[:space:]]*)($DEBT)" 2>/dev/null | awk -F: '{s+=$NF} END{print s+0}'
